# The spec and the plan embed source files verbatim in fenced code blocks, and
# the review process checks those fences byte-for-byte against the committed
# files. Prettier formats embedded code for languages it can parse — verified
# here: it rewrites ```yaml and ```json fences (collapsing indentation, turning
# `[ main ]` into `[main]`) while leaving ```go, ```toml, and ```bash alone.
# That is silent drift in exactly the artifact whose value is being identical to
# the repo, and Task 21 embeds .github/workflows/ci.yml, so it is not theoretical.
#
# This file is only half the guard. Prettier resolves .prettierignore relative
# to the process CWD, so it does nothing when prettier is invoked from outside
# this repo — which is the common case here, since the editor hook that runs it
# does not use the repo root as its CWD. The load-bearing guard is the in-file
# `<!-- prettier-ignore -->` marker above each yaml/json fence. This file only
# covers running prettier from the repo root by hand.
#
# Keeping docs/ unformatted costs nothing: this is a Go repo with no other
# prettier consumer.
docs/
